  {"name":"Edge: very long input (1000 chars)","input":"The network engineer reported that server web-prod-01.datacenter-eu.internal (IP 10.42.88.7) experienced a critical failure at 03:45 UTC. The root cause was traced to a misconfigured BGP session with peer 10.0.0.2 (AS 65002). During the incident, alerts were sent to admin@noc.internal and ops-team@emergency.corp-internal.net. The on-call engineer (phone +353861234567) responded within 5 minutes. Recovery involved resetting the BGP neighbor, clearing the ARP cache, and restarting the OSPF process. The SNMP trap host at 10.1.0.5 confirmed the recovery. Post-incident, the team updated the ACL on the border router to prevent similar misconfigurations. The firewall rules on fw-edge-01.datacenter-eu.internal were also reviewed. Database connections to postgresql://dbadmin:Str0ngP4ss@db-primary.internal:5432/production were verified. The monitoring dashboard at https://grafana.internal-corp.net:3000 showed normal metrics after recovery. Public status page at https://status.example.com was updated.","assertions":{"llm_must_not_see":["10.42.88.7","admin@noc.internal","+353861234567","10.1.0.5","Str0ngP4ss"],"llm_must_see":["status.example.com"],"entity_count_min":8,"no_cgnat_leak":true,"roundtrip":true}},
